= Reich Intervention in Saxony

On 29 October, President Ebert uses his emergency powers against Saxony. Troops march into Dresden and a Reich commissioner removes Zeigner's government. Thuringia's <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span> ministers leave office soon afterwards. The Bavarian government, openly defying Berlin from the right, faces no such action.

The <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> left the Stresemann cabinet in protest. Many <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> workers are angry at their own leaders, which is a small opening for the united front.
